INT. BOWLING ALLEY - LANE 9 - ARBITRATION HEARING - DAY

A defunct bowling alley, repurposed. Folding tables over the gutters. A pin-setting machine looms behind the panel like a sleeping beast.

ARBITRATOR HELENA MBEKI, sixties, reading glasses on a chain, presides from the scoring desk. At the left table: attorney SUNITA KAPOOR, forties, crisp navy suit. At the right: attorney CONRAD ASHWORTH, fifties, rumpled tweed. In the witness chair, a plastic bowling seat: DMITRI VOLKOV, sixties, retired foreman, hands folded. At a small side table, court reporter PAULINA ZAJAC, twenties, fingers poised.

Quiet. Pins rattle faintly somewhere behind a wall.

HELENA
We are on the record. Mr. Volkov, you've been sworn.

DMITRI
I have.

SUNITA
Mr. Volkov, thank you for coming. I'd like to ask about the night of the fourteenth.

DMITRI
Of course.

SUNITA
You were foreman on the closing shift at the Calloway plant?

DMITRI
Twenty-two years.

SUNITA
And that night, you signed the safety log?

DMITRI
I did. As I always did.

SUNITA
Was the lockout valve on press four engaged?

DMITRI
It was.

CONRAD
Objection. Leading.

HELENA
Overruled, Mr. Ashworth. She is asking for a fact.

CONRAD
Then I'll hold my fire, Madam Arbitrator.

SUNITA
Mr. Volkov. Was the valve engaged?

DMITRI
Yes.

SUNITA
You're certain.

DMITRI
I checked it with my own hand.

SUNITA
And yet the incident report states that press four cycled at eleven forty.

DMITRI
It did.

SUNITA
How is that possible if the valve was engaged?

DMITRI
Because I disengaged it at eleven thirty-five.

PAULINA
(quietly)
Could the witness repeat that?

DMITRI
I disengaged it at eleven thirty-five.

CONRAD
Madam Arbitrator, may we have a moment?

HELENA
No. Mr. Volkov, why would you do that?

DMITRI
Because Mr. Calloway's son told me to. He said the order was behind. He said nobody would be near it.

SUNITA
Was anyone near it?

DMITRI
(long pause)
My nephew. Nikolai. He was cleaning the die.

HELENA
Ms. Kapoor, do you have further questions?

SUNITA
Only one. Mr. Volkov, why did you sign the log?

DMITRI
Because they said they would pay for his hospital. And I did not know how to say no.

CONRAD
I withdraw my objection. And I withdraw my client's motion.

HELENA
Mr. Ashworth?

CONRAD
My client wishes to settle.

HELENA
Ms. Zajac, strike nothing.

PAULINA
Yes, ma'am.

HELENA
We are adjourned.
